# AXONTIMEHR — PHASE 11 DEVELOPMENT PROMPT

# EMPLOYEE SELF-SERVICE (ESS), MANAGER SELF-SERVICE (MSS), MOBILE/PWA, COMMUNICATION, DOCUMENTS & EMPLOYEE EXPERIENCE

---

# 1. ROLE

You are acting as a:

* Principal Software Architect
* Senior Full-Stack Engineer
* HRMS Product Architect
* Backend Engineer
* Frontend Engineer
* Mobile/PWA Architect
* PostgreSQL Database Architect
* Security Engineer
* API Architect
* QA Automation Engineer
* DevOps Engineer
* UX/UI Engineer

You are continuing development of **AxonTimeHR**, a production-ready, enterprise-grade, multi-tenant Attendance + HRMS SaaS platform.

Your task is to implement **PHASE 11** completely while preserving all functionality from Phases 1–10.

---

# 2. EXISTING PHASES

Assume the following phases are already implemented:

```text
Phase 1  — Foundation
Phase 2  — Authentication + Identity + RBAC
Phase 3  — Organization + Employee Management
Phase 4  — Attendance + Shift Management
Phase 5  — GPS + Geofencing + Verified Attendance
Phase 6  — Leave + Holiday + Regularization + Approval Workflow
Phase 7  — Payroll + Salary + Compensation
Phase 8  — Expense + Reimbursement + Loan + Salary Advance
Phase 9  — Performance + Goals/KPIs + Appraisal + 360 Feedback
           + Training + Learning + Employee Engagement
Phase 10 — Recruitment / ATS + Workforce Planning
           + Advanced HR Analytics + AI HR Intelligence
```

---

# 3. CRITICAL RULE

## DO NOT REBUILD EXISTING FUNCTIONALITY

Before writing code:

1. Inspect the complete repository.
2. Understand the existing architecture.
3. Understand database conventions.
4. Understand authentication.
5. Understand RBAC.
6. Understand tenant isolation.
7. Understand employee relationships.
8. Understand attendance.
9. Understand leave.
10. Understand payroll.
11. Understand expenses.
12. Understand performance.
13. Understand recruitment.
14. Understand analytics.
15. Understand notifications.
16. Understand file storage.
17. Understand audit logging.
18. Understand background jobs.
19. Understand frontend architecture.
20. Understand existing responsive/mobile behavior.
21. Understand existing API conventions.
22. Understand existing testing.

Then extend the system.

---

# 4. PHASE 11 OBJECTIVE

Build a comprehensive:

# EMPLOYEE EXPERIENCE PLATFORM

including:

```text
Employee Self-Service
Manager Self-Service
Employee Dashboard
Mobile/PWA Experience
Attendance Self-Service
Leave Self-Service
Payroll Self-Service
Expense Self-Service
Loan/Advance Self-Service
Performance Self-Service
Training Self-Service
Recruitment/Onboarding Self-Service
Employee Documents
Digital HR Letters
HR Requests
Helpdesk
Announcements
Internal Communication
Employee Directory
Organization Directory
Employee Profile
Emergency Contacts
Asset Visibility
Notifications Center
Approvals Center
Tasks
Calendar
Employee Timeline
Mobile Notifications
Offline-capable PWA Foundation
```

The objective is to reduce HR dependency for routine employee operations.

