# 33. DIGITAL HR LETTERS

Support HR-generated documents:

```text
Offer Letter
Appointment Letter
Experience Letter
Promotion Letter
Salary Revision Letter
Warning Letter where applicable
Transfer Letter
Relieving Letter
Other HR Letters
```

Use configurable templates.

---

# 34. DOCUMENT TEMPLATE ENGINE

Create reusable document templates.

Templates may contain variables:

```text
{{employee_name}}
{{employee_id}}
{{designation}}
{{department}}
{{joining_date}}
{{salary}}
{{manager_name}}
{{organization_name}}
```

Do not expose template internals to unauthorized employees.

---

# 35. DOCUMENT GENERATION

Document workflow:

```text
Template
 ↓
Employee Data
 ↓
Generate Document
 ↓
Review
 ↓
Approve if required
 ↓
Store
 ↓
Employee Access
```

Store a generated-document snapshot.

If employee data changes later, previously issued documents must not silently change.

---

# 36. DOCUMENT VERSIONING

Maintain:

```text
Document Version
Generated At
Generated By
Template Version
Status
```

Issued documents should be immutable.

---

# 37. ELECTRONIC ACKNOWLEDGEMENT

Allow employees to acknowledge documents.

Store:

```text
Employee
Document
Acknowledged
Acknowledged At
Comment
```

Where legally appropriate, support an extensible signature/acknowledgement architecture.

Do not claim legally binding e-signature functionality unless a compliant signature provider is integrated.

