# 59. MOBILE / PWA

Build a Progressive Web App layer if compatible with the existing React architecture.

Requirements:

```text
Installable
Responsive
Mobile-friendly
Secure
Fast
Offline-aware
```

Do not create a separate mobile codebase unless there is a strong reason.

---

# 60. PWA MANIFEST

Configure:

```text
App Name
Short Name
Icons
Theme
Start URL
Display Mode
```

Use the existing frontend build system.

---

# 61. SERVICE WORKER

If implementing service workers:

Use them carefully.

Cache:

```text
Static Assets
Application Shell
Safe Read-Only Resources
```

Do NOT cache sensitive responses indiscriminately.

Avoid storing:

```text
Payslips
Salary Data
Private HR Documents
Sensitive Employee Data
```

in insecure client caches.

---

# 62. OFFLINE MODE

Provide limited offline capability.

Potentially support:

```text
View basic cached shell
View non-sensitive previously loaded information
Queue safe actions where appropriate
```

Do NOT blindly queue sensitive transactions.

For attendance:

```text
Offline Check-In
```

should only be implemented if the backend has a secure reconciliation mechanism.

Never fabricate timestamps or GPS data.

---

# 63. MOBILE SECURITY

Protect:

* Authentication tokens
* Cached data
* Documents
* Payslips
* Personal information
* Location information

Use secure browser storage patterns.

Do not store sensitive authentication material in insecure local storage if the architecture can avoid it.

---

# 64. SESSION MANAGEMENT

Support:

```text
Active Sessions
Device Information
Last Active
Logout Session
Logout All Sessions
```

Use the existing authentication infrastructure.

Do not create a second identity system.

---

# 65. DEVICE MANAGEMENT

Where supported, show:

```text
Browser
Device
Last Active
Approximate Location where legally/technically appropriate
Session Status
```

Allow user to revoke sessions.

