Adapt routes to existing conventions.

---

# 77. "ME" API SECURITY

The `/me` API must determine the employee from the authenticated identity.

Do not trust:

```text
employee_id
```

sent by the frontend to access another employee's information.

Correct:

```text
JWT/session
 ↓
Authenticated User
 ↓
Linked Employee
 ↓
Employee Data
```

---

# 78. API PAGINATION

Paginate:

```text
Notifications
Documents
Requests
Tickets
Announcements
Directory
Tasks
History
```

Never return unbounded datasets.

---

# 79. API FILTERING

Support appropriate:

```text
Date Range
Status
Category
Department
Location
Priority
```

But enforce authorization before filtering.

---

# 80. DATABASE DESIGN

Inspect existing models first.

Potential Phase 11 tables:

```text
employee_profile_change_requests

employee_documents
document_templates
document_versions
document_acknowledgements

hr_policies
policy_versions
policy_acknowledgements

hr_requests
hr_request_comments

helpdesk_tickets
helpdesk_comments
helpdesk_attachments

announcements
announcement_audiences
announcement_reads
announcement_acknowledgements

employee_recognitions

employee_privacy_settings

onboarding_tasks
onboarding_task_assignments

employee_sessions

notification_preferences
```

Do not create duplicates of existing notification, document, workflow, or employee tables.

---

# 81. DATABASE CONSTRAINTS

Use:

* Foreign keys
* Unique constraints
* Check constraints
* Tenant constraints
* Appropriate indexes

Maintain historical data.

---

# 82. TENANT ISOLATION

Every tenant-owned resource must enforce tenant isolation.

Never allow:

```text
Tenant A Employee
 ↓
Tenant B Document
```

or:

```text
Tenant A User
 ↓
Tenant B Announcement
```

---

# 83. RBAC

Reuse the existing authorization system.

Potential permissions:

```text
self.profile.view
self.profile.update
self.documents.view
self.documents.download
self.requests.create
self.requests.view
self.helpdesk.create
self.helpdesk.view
self.announcements.view

team.view
team.approvals
team.attendance.view
team.leave.view
team.performance.view

documents.manage
announcements.manage
policies.manage
helpdesk.manage
```

Use existing naming conventions.

---

# 84. MANAGER SCOPE

A manager may access only employees within their authorized hierarchy.

Do not rely solely on:

```text
manager_id == current_user.employee_id
```

if the organization supports:

* Multiple levels
* Matrix reporting
* Delegation
* Temporary managers
* Department scopes

Use the existing organizational authorization model.

---

# 85. APPROVAL DELEGATION

If the existing approval system supports delegation, integrate it.

Example:

```text
Manager unavailable
 ↓
Delegated Approver
 ↓
Approval
```

Do not create a separate delegation system unless necessary.

---

# 86. DOCUMENT SECURITY

Document downloads must validate:

```text
Authenticated User
Tenant
Document Ownership
Permission
Document Status
```

Do not expose storage URLs directly if that bypasses authorization.

Use secure access mechanisms.

---

# 87. AUDIT LOGGING

Audit:

```text
Profile Change Request
Profile Update
Document Upload
Document Download where required
Document Acknowledgement
Policy Acknowledgement
HR Request
Ticket
Announcement
Recognition
Session Revocation
Notification Preference Changes
```

---

# 88. SENSITIVE DATA AUDIT

Pay special attention to:

```text
Salary
Payslips
Bank Information
Emergency Contacts
Personal Address
Identity Documents
HR Documents
Performance Records
Private HR Tickets
```

Do not expose them through generic employee APIs.

---

# 89. BACKGROUND JOBS

Reuse Celery/Redis.

Possible jobs:

```text
Document expiry reminders
Policy acknowledgement reminders
Announcement notifications
HR request reminders
Helpdesk SLA reminders
Training reminders
Onboarding reminders
Birthday/anniversary notifications where enabled
```

Jobs must be:

* Idempotent
* Retry-safe
* Logged
* Tenant-aware

---

# 90. NOTIFICATIONS

Integrate existing notification service.

Examples:

```text
Leave Approved
Expense Approved
Payslip Available
Document Uploaded
Policy Requires Acknowledgement
HR Request Updated
Ticket Updated
Training Assigned
Performance Review Opened
Announcement Published
```

---

# 91. EMAIL

Reuse existing email infrastructure.

Add templates where required:

```text
HR Request Created
HR Request Updated
Ticket Created
Ticket Updated
Document Available
Policy Acknowledgement Required
Announcement
Onboarding Reminder
```

---

# 92. PUSH NOTIFICATIONS

If the existing architecture supports push notifications, integrate it.

Do not make push notifications mandatory for core web functionality.

---

# 93. OFFLINE SYNCHRONIZATION

If offline actions are supported:

Use a controlled queue:

```text
Local Action
 ↓
Action ID
 ↓
Sync Queue
 ↓
Server
 ↓
Idempotency Check
 ↓
Validation
 ↓
Commit
 ↓
Sync Result
```

Never blindly replay actions.

---

# 94. IDEMPOTENCY

Protect against duplicate requests.

Especially:

```text
Leave Submission
Expense Submission
HR Request
Ticket Creation
Document Upload
Attendance Check-In
Attendance Check-Out
Profile Change
```

Use existing idempotency architecture if present.

---

# 95. CONCURRENCY

Protect:

```text
Duplicate approvals
Duplicate submissions
Duplicate attendance events
Duplicate document generation
Duplicate employee onboarding completion
```

Use:

* Transactions
* Unique constraints
* Locking where appropriate
* Idempotency

---

# 96. PERFORMANCE

Optimize:

* Employee dashboard
* Notification center
* Directory
* Document center
* Manager dashboard
* Approval inbox
* Mobile API

Avoid N+1 queries.

Use optimized backend aggregation.

---

# 97. MOBILE API OPTIMIZATION

Mobile clients should receive compact payloads.

Avoid returning huge objects.

Provide dashboard aggregation endpoints where useful.

Example:

```text
GET /api/v1/me/dashboard
```

can return a controlled summary.

---

# 98. SECURITY HEADERS

Ensure frontend/backend use appropriate security controls.

Examples:

```text
HTTPS
Secure Cookies where applicable
HttpOnly Cookies where applicable
Content Security Policy
X-Content-Type-Options
Frame protection
Referrer policy
```

Adapt to existing infrastructure.

---

# 99. RATE LIMITING

Protect:

```text
Login
OTP if used
Public recruitment
HR requests
Ticket creation
Document operations
Notification APIs
Search
```

Reuse existing rate-limiting infrastructure.

---

# 100. FILE UPLOAD SECURITY

For employee documents:

Validate:

```text
Extension
MIME
File Size
Content Type
Filename
```

Prevent:

```text
Executable uploads
Path traversal
Malicious filenames
Cross-tenant access
Unauthorized download
```

---

# 101. DATA VALIDATION

Use Pydantic/backend validation.

Never trust frontend validation alone.

Validate:

```text
Dates
Phone
Email
File metadata
Request type
Status transitions
Employee ownership
Document ownership
```

---

# 102. HR REQUEST WORKFLOW

Use existing workflow engine where possible.

Do not implement hard-coded approval chains inside frontend components.

---

# 103. HELP DESK SLA

Create an extensible SLA structure.

Potential configuration:

```text
Priority
Response Time
Resolution Time
Escalation
```

If full SLA automation is too large for this phase, implement the data model and service architecture for future expansion.

---

# 104. ANNOUNCEMENT SCHEDULING

Allow HR to schedule announcements.

Example:

```text
Draft
 ↓
Scheduled
 ↓
Published
 ↓
Expired
```

Background jobs should publish/expire them.

---

# 105. ANNOUNCEMENT PRIORITY

Support:

```text
NORMAL
IMPORTANT
URGENT
```

Urgent notifications should be carefully controlled.

Do not spam employees.

---

# 106. EMPLOYEE SEARCH PRIVACY

Do not expose:

* Personal phone unless allowed
* Personal email unless allowed
* Home address
* Bank details
* Salary
* Performance details
* Emergency contacts

through directory APIs.

---

# 107. PROFILE DATA SEPARATION

Separate:

```text
Public Work Profile
Private Personal Profile
Sensitive HR Profile
Payroll Profile
```

Use different authorization boundaries.

---

# 108. API RESPONSE DESIGN

Use existing response standards.

Example:

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "data": {},
  "message": "Request submitted successfully"
}
```

For errors:

```json
{
  "success": false,
  "message": "You are not authorized to access this document",
  "error_code": "DOCUMENT_ACCESS_DENIED"
}
```

Never expose stack traces.

---

# 109. FRONTEND STATE MANAGEMENT

Reuse existing state-management patterns.

Do not introduce a new state-management library unless necessary.

---

# 110. TYPESCRIPT

Use strict types.

Avoid unnecessary:

```typescript
any
```

Create types for:

```text
Employee
Profile
Document
HRRequest
Ticket
Announcement
Notification
Task
Approval
Policy
Recognition
```

---

# 111. GLOBAL TASK CENTER

Create a reusable task aggregation component.

Example:

```text
My Tasks
-------------------------
Leave Approval        2
Expense Approval      3
Performance Review    1
Policy Acknowledgement 2
Training              1
HR Request            1
```

Each item deep-links into the correct module.

---

# 112. EMPLOYEE DASHBOARD WIDGETS

Widgets should be configurable.

Possible widgets:

```text
Attendance
Leave
Payslip
Tasks
Notifications
Goals
Training
Documents
Announcements
```

Allow future tenant customization.

---

# 113. MOBILE DASHBOARD

Prioritize:

```text
Attendance
Leave
Tasks
Notifications
Payslip
Requests
Profile
```

Keep mobile dashboard lightweight.

---

# 114. PWA INSTALLATION

Provide install experience where browser/platform supports it.

Do not block users who do not install the PWA.

The normal browser application must continue working.

---

# 115. MOBILE ERROR HANDLING

Handle:

```text
Offline
Slow Network
Expired Session
Permission Denied
Location Permission Denied
Server Error
Upload Failure
```

Provide clear recovery actions.

---

# 116. ACCESSIBILITY ON MOBILE

Ensure:

* Touch targets are usable
* Forms are readable
* Text scales appropriately
* Keyboard does not hide important controls
* Dialogs are accessible

---

# 117. TESTING — UNIT

Create tests for:

```text
Profile permissions
Change request workflow
Document permissions
Policy acknowledgement
HR request lifecycle
Announcement targeting
Notification preferences
Task aggregation
Directory filtering
Session revocation
```

---

# 118. API TESTING

Test:

```text
Authentication
Authorization
Tenant isolation
Employee ownership
Manager scope
Pagination
Filtering
Validation
Error handling
Idempotency
```

---

# 119. SECURITY TESTING

Explicitly test:

### IDOR

Change document/request/employee IDs.

Expected:

```text
403 / 404
```

### Cross-Tenant

Attempt access to another tenant.

Expected:

```text
403 / 404
```

### Employee → HR

Employee must not access HR-only APIs.

### Manager Scope

Manager cannot access unauthorized employees.

### Payslip Security

Employee cannot access another employee's payslip.

### Document Security

Employee cannot access another employee's private document.

---

# 120. FILE SECURITY TESTS

Attempt:

```text
Executable upload
Invalid MIME
Oversized file
Path traversal
Unauthorized download
Cross-tenant download
```

All must be rejected or safely handled.

---

# 121. NOTIFICATION TESTS

Verify:

```text
Notification creation
Read/unread
Mark all read
Deep links
Authorization
Tenant isolation
Preferences
Duplicate prevention
```

---

# 122. PWA TESTING

Test:

```text
Installability
Responsive layout
Service worker
Cache behavior
Offline shell
Session expiry
Network recovery
```

Ensure sensitive data is not unintentionally cached.

---

# 123. MOBILE ATTENDANCE TESTING

Test:

```text
Location allowed
Location denied
Inside geofence
Outside geofence
Selfie verification
Network failure
Duplicate check-in
Duplicate check-out
```

---

